Requirements Design Specification: Request-Based Approval System

1. Introduction

This document describes the requirements and high-level design for a four-level request-approval system. The workflow advances a request through the following roles:

Staff

Manager

Director

CEO

Each request includes a category and a free-form reason. Images are optional (not in initial phase). Approvers can approve or reject; approvals move requests up, rejections move them back.

2. Purpose and Scope

Purpose: Provide clear requirements and design guidance for implementing a robust, extensible approval workflow.

Scope:

Creation and submission of requests by Staff

Multi-level review and approval

Status tracking and notifications

Audit trail of decisions

Role-based access control

Excluded: image handling (deferred), integrations (e.g. email), reporting dashboard.

3. Stakeholders

Staff: Submit requests, view status

Manager/Director/CEO: Review, approve, or reject requests

System Administrator: Configure categories, manage users and roles

Business Owner: Ensures workflow meets policy requirements

