5. Non-Functional Requirements

NFR-01 Security: All endpoints require authentication; role-based authorization.

NFR-02 Performance: Listing and status queries must return within 500ms under typical load.

NFR-03 Scalability: Design for eventual addition of more approval levels.

NFR-04 Usability: Simple, intuitive interfaces with clear status indicators.

NFR-05 Auditability: Immutable audit log stored in relational database.

6. High-Level Data Model

-- Users and Roles
CREATE TABLE User (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY,
  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
  email VARCHAR(150) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  role ENUM('Staff','Manager','Director','CEO') NOT NULL
);

-- Requests
CREATE TABLE Request (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  creator_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES User(id),
  category VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
  reason TEXT NOT NULL,
  status ENUM(
    'Pending_Manager',
    'Rejected_Manager',
    'Pending_Director',
    'Rejected_Director',
    'Pending_CEO',
    'Rejected_CEO',
    'Approved'
  ) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Pending_Manager',
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  updated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- Approval History
CREATE TABLE ApprovalHistory (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  request_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES Request(id),
  approver_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES User(id),
  action ENUM('Approve','Reject') NOT NULL,
  comments TEXT,
  action_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

7. Workflow Diagram

[Staff creates Request]
        |
        v
[Pending_Manager] --Approve--> [Pending_Director]
        | Reject                      |
        v                             v
[Rejected_Manager]              [Pending_Director] --Approve--> [Pending_CEO]
                                             | Reject                    |
                                             v                           v
                                  [Rejected_Director]           [Pending_CEO] --Approve--> [Approved]
                                                                        | Reject
                                                                        v
                                                                 [Rejected_CEO]

8. API Endpoints

Authentication

POST /auth/login – authenticate, return JWT

Requests

POST /requests – create (Staff only)

GET /requests?filter= – list user’s or role’s pending requests

GET /requests/{id} – get details + history

Approval Actions

POST /requests/{id}/approve – approve (Manager/Director/CEO)

Body: { comments?: string }\

POST /requests/{id}/reject – reject

Body: { comments: string }\

Responses return updated status and history.

9. User Interfaces

Staff Portal

Button: "New Request"

Table: My Requests (columns: ID, Category, Created At, Status)

Approver Dashboard

Filter: "Pending for Me"

List: clickable rows to detail view

Detail: reason text, history log, Approve/Reject buttons + comments

